


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Find the exact value of each of the following without using technology. Angles are in radians unless specifically marked as degrees.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\sin(150^\circ)</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\sin(150^\circ) = \dfrac{1}{2}</m>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\cos\pbr{\dfrac{4\pi}{3}}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\cos\pbr{\dfrac{4\pi}{3}} = -\dfrac{1}{2}</m>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{-\dfrac{\pi}{4}}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{-\dfrac{\pi}{4}} = \dfrac{-\sqrt{2} }{2} </m>

<em>You can use the idea that <m>-\pi /4</m> radians is the same as <m>-45^\circ </m> and go clockwise on the unit circle, or compute a coterminal angle to <m>-\pi /4</m> that is between <m>0</m> and <m>2\pi </m> radians. This coterminal angle is <m>7\pi /4</m>.</em>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{\dfrac{2\pi}{3}}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{\dfrac{2\pi}{3}} = \dfrac{\sqrt{3} }{2} </m>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\sin(315^\circ)</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\sin(315^\circ) = \dfrac{-\sqrt{2} }{2} </m>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{\dfrac{13\pi}{6}}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{\dfrac{13\pi}{6}} = \dfrac{1}{2}</m> \qquad <em>A coterminal angle to <m>13\pi /6</m> is <m>\pi /6</m>.</em>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{\dfrac{7\pi}{3}}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\sin\pbr{\dfrac{7\pi}{3}} = \dfrac{\sqrt{3} }{2}  </m> \qquad <em>A coterminal angle to <m>\frac{7\pi}{3}</m> is <m>\frac{\pi}{3}</m>.</em>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\cos(-30^\circ)</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\cos(-30^\circ) = \dfrac{\sqrt{3} }{2} </m>  \qquad <em>A coterminal angle to <m>-30^\circ </m> is <m>330^\circ </m>.</em>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>\cos(210^\circ)</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
<m>\cos(210^\circ) = \dfrac{-\sqrt{3} }{2} </m>
</p>
</solution>
</task>




</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
Use a calculator to find approximate values for <m>\sin(5)</m> and <m>\cos(5)</m> for <m>5</m> degrees and for <m>5</m> radians.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
In radians, <m>\sin (5) = -0.9589</m> and <m>\cos (5) = 0.2837</m>.

In degrees, <m>\sin (5^\circ ) = 0.0872</m> and <m>\cos (5^\circ ) = 0.9962</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>
